---
/** Slide 02 · The hook — the exit problem. */
import InlineCitation from '@components/citations/InlineCitation.astro';
import { CITE } from './citations';
---

<section data-slot="02" data-variant="rib-p1" class="deck-section deck-glow" style="align-items: center; text-align: center;">
  <span class="deck-kicker">02 / 11</span>

  <p class="deck-eyebrow">The hook</p>
  <h2 class="deck-h1" style="max-width: 22ch;">
    Rural America doesn't have a talent shortage. It has an exit problem —
    <span class="deck-gradient">every credential is a bus ticket out.</span>
  </h2>
  <p class="deck-lede" style="max-width: 64ch; margin-inline: auto;">
    The loop is self-reinforcing: chronic shortages (teachers first, then
    healthcare), no affordable local path to a degree, and the steady
    out-migration of anyone who earns one — exporting both the talent and the
    income it would have spent locally.<InlineCitation {...CITE.get('542c7f')!} />
  </p>
</section>
